{"kind":"request","text":"OPS-2: the `dap` command installs from one package, without a\ncheckout\n\nItem 5 of order act fc7576f8. Today docs/get-dap.md tells a user to\nclone the repository and run `npm ci`. The package\n`@generalbusiness/dap-cli` is private, runs its TypeScript source\nthrough tsx (bin/dap.js:7), and depends on eight workspace packages.\nTwo of them, dap-scope and dap-mcp, are not in the release plan of\nscripts/public-release.json. One head. It publishes nothing.\n\nDecision: bundle. The CLI ships one built file that holds its\nworkspace packages, including the scope runtime and the MCP server.\ndap-scope and dap-mcp do not become public packages, because\ndap-scope carries the Worker code.\n\n1. A build step makes one `dist` entry for the `dap` command from\n   `src/main.ts` with the esbuild that the package already pins.\n   The installed command starts with plain Node and no TypeScript\n   loader. State the Node version that the built file needs.\n2. Keep what the command loads at run time as ordinary\n   dependencies, and say why for each one. `dap dev` and `dap\n   check` read an author's files. If they need esbuild or tsx at\n   run time, keep that dependency. If they do not, remove it.\n3. package.json: `files`, `private` false, the bin entries on the\n   built file, and no workspace package in `dependencies`.\n4. Add the CLI to the release plan as a tenth entry with its\n   bundle step. The producer and the checker cover it:\n   scripts/public-release.mjs and scripts/check-public-release.mjs.\n5. The checkout path still works: a contributor runs the command\n   from source as today, and the tests do not need a build first.\n\nWitness: the checker's script installs the staged tarball in an\nempty directory outside the checkout, with no network access to\nthis repository. `dap` with no arguments prints the usage text and\nexits 2, as the source command does. `dap new`, `dap check` and\n`dap pack` run on a fresh package in that directory and give the\nresults that docs/cli.md states. Name each command that cannot run\nfrom the installed package, with its reason.\n\nOut of scope: publication to npm, the version number of the first\npublic release, and docs/get-dap.md. The namespace owner publishes\nafter the identifiers cutover, so that the first public command\nspeaks the new identifiers. I revise the page with that release.\n\nPaths: packages/cli/package.json, packages/cli/bin, a build\nscript, scripts/public-release.json, scripts/public-release.mjs,\nscripts/check-public-release.mjs and their tests. Report any\nshared path with heads G, H or JP1 before you start. Gate once at\nthe head. Checker review at the exact head. No deployment.","body":{"conditions":"The dap command builds to one file that holds its workspace packages; @generalbusiness/dap-cli is a tenth entry of the release plan with files, bin and no workspace dependency; the staged tarball installs in an empty directory outside the checkout and dap, dap new, dap check and dap pack run there; the source path still works. Nothing is published. Gate at the head, checker review, no deployment.","target_head":"166150ab68fe4fdf1a58920a6fab323015839546","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}